//
// @FR-N-Decl — a copy of a declared `vector<u8>` constant refuses an element a `u8` cannot
// hold, as a `vector<u8>` local does; with the annotation discarded it took `300` (loft#2240).
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot implicitly narrow integer to u8
//
// @falsified-at: 6184655a5 — interpret exit 1 -> 0, interpret expectations FAIL/1 -> 0/1,
//   native exit 1 -> 0, native expectations FAIL/1 -> 0/1: the control accepted the 300 and
//   printed [1,2,300].
//   HOLDS: assertions, leak, panic, refusals are equal on both trees.

CV: vector<u8> = [1, 2];

fn main() {
  v = CV;
  v += [300];
  println("{v}");
}
